1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,760
The framework gives six postures: own the
outcome, stay close to reality, act to learn, know

2
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:09,585
what you know, trade off on purpose,
and leave capability behind.

3
00:00:09,655 --> 00:00:11,617
Apply them to an actual choice.

4
00:00:11,687 --> 00:00:17,213
Ask whose result matters, what you observed,
which experiment reduces uncertainty, which

5
00:00:17,283 --> 00:00:22,701
claims remain assumptions, what risk you are
accepting, and what will remain useful when you

6
00:00:22,771 --> 00:00:29,086
leave. A principle becomes practical when it
changes scope, evidence, authority, or sequencing.

7
00:00:29,156 --> 00:00:32,249
The sponsor requests
automatic replies this Friday.

8
00:00:32,319 --> 00:00:38,058
You have permission to analyze synthetic tickets
but no authority to send customer messages.

9
00:00:38,128 --> 00:00:41,371
Maya agrees to test
suggestions with human review.

10
00:00:41,441 --> 00:00:45,089
The security reviewer has not
assessed production data access.

11
00:00:45,159 --> 00:00:49,937
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

12
00:00:50,007 --> 00:00:51,799
Select a Friday deliverable.

13
00:00:51,869 --> 00:00:56,179
Explain its learning value, authority
boundary, and reusable output.

14
00:00:56,249 --> 00:01:01,241
Deliver one synthetic ticket flowing through
a routing rule, a review screen, and an

15
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,761
observable decision.

16
00:01:02,831 --> 00:01:05,498
Record a prediction about review usefulness.

17
00:01:05,568 --> 00:01:07,125
Do not send messages.

18
00:01:07,195 --> 00:01:10,566
Keep the data validation
and audit helper reusable.

19
00:01:10,636 --> 00:01:16,439
This accepts limited scope and avoids committing
the organization to an unreviewed action

20
00:01:16,509 --> 00:01:20,882
channel. It also creates a measurable
question for the next experiment.

21
00:01:20,952 --> 00:01:23,235
Which choice respects the permission boundary?

22
00:01:23,305 --> 00:01:26,910
A. Send replies because the
sponsor requested speed B.

23
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:30,095
Use production data without telling security C.

24
00:01:30,165 --> 00:01:33,322
Test a reviewable suggestion
with permitted data.

25
00:01:33,392 --> 00:01:34,800
The best answer is C.

26
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:36,897
Speed does not expand authority.

27
00:01:36,967 --> 00:01:40,252
The permitted experiment still
produces useful evidence.
